# Keeps the build context small, the build reproducible, and secrets out of the
# image. The context is the repo root (`docker build .`, and `context: ..` in
# deploy/docker-compose.yml), so without this file every local node_modules and
# target directory would be uploaded to the daemon on every build.
#
# Three different jobs here, and the middle one is the easy one to miss.

# --- Secrets. Never in an image, however convenient. --------------------------
# deploy/.env holds a real CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY on a working machine. The
# whole deploy/ directory is excluded below too, but this is stated separately
# because it must survive someone later deciding they need deploy/ in the context.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks

# --- Build output that the image rebuilds itself. -----------------------------
# This is the load-bearing part. frontend/dist and backend/target exist on any
# machine that has run the app locally, and both are *also* produced inside the
# build. Leaving them in the context means a stale local bundle can be copied
# over the freshly built one, producing an image that serves a frontend nobody
# compiled from the committed source - and it fails silently, looking only like a
# change that "didn't take".
**/node_modules
**/target
frontend/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage

# --- Everything the build has no use for. -------------------------------------
# Excluded to keep the context small and, more usefully, to stop edits to docs or
# CI config from invalidating Docker's layer cache and triggering a full rebuild.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea
docs
evals
harness
deploy
README.md
LICENSE
*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# --- Local noise. -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
